{
  "description": "1) Rebuilding a rear garden extension and in London stock brick to replace the existing ground level glass and timber extension. This includes a new pitched roof with skylights to the rear and side return.\n2) New rear extension with a slate finish at second floor/roof level (‘pod’ extension). Aligned with neighbour (3 Wardo Ave) pod extension. 2 windows and skylight to this new rear mansard extension.\n3) Existing pitched roof over existing 1st floor level replaced with flat roof accessible from pod extension with obscured minimum 1.7 m high balustrade to perimeter of flat roof.\n4) Refurbish existing roof. Solar panels to flat roof where possible. Fall arrest system (mansafe) to be installed to flat roof for safe access and maintenance. \n5) New window to side elevation at first floor level. Obscured and fixed glazing up to 1.7m above internal FFL.\n6) Gate and pier to front boundary wall on street for improved access to bins.\n",
